            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33762",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/go-git/go-git/v5: go-git: Denial of Service via crafted Git index file"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "go-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. Prior to version 5.17.1, go-git’s index decoder for format version 4 fails to validate the path name prefix length before applying it to the previously decoded path name. A maliciously crafted index file can trigger an out-of-bounds slice operation, resulting in a runtime panic during normal index parsing. This issue only affects Git index format version 4. Earlier formats (go-git supports only v2 and v3) are not vulnerable to this issue. This issue has been patched in version 5.17.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33762",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-33762\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/go-git/go-git/v5\nFixed Version: 5.17.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-33762](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33762)\ngo-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. Prior to version 5.17.1, go-git’s index decoder for format version 4 fails to validate the path name prefix length before applying it to the previously decoded path name. A maliciously crafted index file can trigger an out-of-bounds slice operation, resulting in a runtime panic during normal index parsing. This issue only affects Git index format version 4. Earlier formats (go-git supports only v2 and v3) are not vulnerable to this issue. This issue has been patched in version 5.17.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-33762**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/go-git/go-git/v5|5.17.1|[CVE-2026-33762](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33762)|\n\ngo-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. Prior to version 5.17.1, go-git’s index decoder for format version 4 fails to validate the path name prefix length before applying it to the previously decoded path name. A maliciously crafted index file can trigger an out-of-bounds slice operation, resulting in a runtime panic during normal index parsing. This issue only affects Git index format version 4. Earlier formats (go-git supports only v2 and v3) are not vulnerable to this issue. This issue has been patched in version 5.17.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 2.8,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
